  "summary_en": "Panama's ten-year national AI strategy (2026–2036) built on six pillars: infrastructure, human capital, data/safety/security, governance, investment, and sectoral application. It favors agile, pro-innovation regulation (sandboxes, ethical impact assessments for high-impact systems) over restrictive rules, with only passing references to robotics, drones and autonomous logistics vehicles.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Rejects restrictive AI regulation in favor of sectoral regulatory sandboxes, e.g., for autonomous delivery drones.",
   "Mandatory Ethical Impact Assessments and human-in-the-loop for AI with significant societal impact.",
   "Creates the National Applied AI Institute as an execution engine, not a regulator.",
   "Enforces Law 81 data rights (ARCO) and strengthens ANTAI oversight.",
   "Explores robotics and autonomous systems in ports, agriculture and manufacturing as a strategic line."
